ems\" loop, because the loop `for (const button of removeButtons) { fireEvent.click(button); }` used a **stale** array of button references captured once before the loop began, causing only 5 of 9 tickets to actually be removed (observed state: `\"Total: 100.00 PLN\"`, 4 remaining 25.00 PLN items) instead of all of them.\n   5. Just applied an `Edit` to fix this by replacing the loop with:\n      ```js\n      while (screen.queryAllByTestId('summary-item-remove-button').length > 0) {\n        fireEvent.click(screen.getAllByTestId('summary-item-remove-button')[0]);\n      }\n      ```\n   This edit was the very last action taken, and its success/failure **has not yet been verified** — the test suite has not been re-run since this fix was applied.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Re-run the test suite to verify the fix for the stale-DOM-reference bug in the removal loop, using the exact command already established in this session: `cd /workspace/project && CI=true pnpm nx test cinescope`. This directly continues the in-progress verification of `flow.smoke.spec.tsx`'s third test case, which was left in an unverified state immediately before this summary was requested. If it passes, the next natural step (per my own stated plan, consistent with the user's original instruction that the task is finished only when all tickets are done and the build succeeds) is to do a final acceptance-criteria review per ticket 07 and a final `pnpm nx build cinescope` confirmation, then decide on the fate of the temporary smoke-test file, all while being mindful of the tight remaining budget (~$2.23 of $5).\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /capture/claude-config/projects/-workspace-project/fc51c61a-6dab-4a2b-8142-c8f64be3453e.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summar